WEBVTT

00:11.010 --> 00:13.720
2500 YEN PER T-SHIRT, ONE SIZE ONLY!

00:11.670 --> 00:13.470
T-shirts! Get your T-shirts here!

00:13.880 --> 00:15.680
We have towels too!

00:15.840 --> 00:17.720
Thank you for your patronage!

00:18.220 --> 00:20.140
Thank you for your...

00:24.520 --> 00:27.610
I told you no one's going to buy this.

00:27.940 --> 00:31.570
Why make them when we haven't
even decided on our band name?

00:31.740 --> 00:35.610
Well y'know, I just thought it could help with our funds and stuff...

00:36.110 --> 00:37.820
What are we, a football team?

00:39.240 --> 00:42.870
Well, if we become famous maybe we can
sell those as an ultra-rare item.

00:43.250 --> 00:44.620
You're being a bit <i>too</i> optimistic there.

00:45.960 --> 00:46.750
Hey.

00:47.540 --> 00:49.630
What're you spacing out for?

00:50.670 --> 00:52.010
<i>Thanks for coming!</i>

00:51.050 --> 00:51.960
I'll be cheering for you!

00:52.420 --> 00:53.550
Do your best.

00:54.050 --> 00:55.880
I'll definitely come to your next concert!

00:56.550 --> 00:58.430
Thank you, I hope to see you there.

01:00.100 --> 01:02.220
Rupa-san's so popular...

01:02.390 --> 01:05.520
That's great and all, but we
really need to decide on our name.

01:05.770 --> 01:07.600
- True.
- You got a moment?

01:10.730 --> 01:11.320
Of course.

02:42.570 --> 02:47.200
I'LL GIVE YOU A NAME

02:42.570 --> 02:47.200
TL Note : The title is a reference to the song of the same name (Namae wo Tsuketeyaru) by Spitz.

02:42.620 --> 02:44.530
- A concert?
- Yep.

02:44.910 --> 02:47.500
Someone who helped me when I was just starting out

02:47.660 --> 02:49.290
was asking if we wanted to play.

02:49.750 --> 02:51.170
Where's the venue?

02:51.670 --> 02:52.830
In Suwa, Nagano.

02:53.130 --> 02:56.380
The plan is to arrive the night before the concert and rehearse right before it.

02:56.550 --> 02:57.960
We're supposed to go back right after,

02:58.130 --> 03:00.800
but I can play alone if you guys are busy.

03:01.090 --> 03:03.800
Nina has studying to do, after all.

03:04.140 --> 03:04.800
We're going!

03:05.180 --> 03:05.680
Right?

03:05.850 --> 03:08.560
Are you serious? We still sound like a
bunch of bickering instruments.

03:08.730 --> 03:11.940
It's fine, the more we'll play the better we'll get.

03:13.060 --> 03:14.810
Well, if you say so...

03:15.360 --> 03:17.340
Which means we’re in.

03:17.460 --> 03:18.740
Alright, alright.

03:19.360 --> 03:20.320
Hmmm...

03:20.990 --> 03:21.700
What is it?

03:22.160 --> 03:25.490
What are we going to do about our name?

03:25.990 --> 03:27.830
THE NEXT DAY

03:27.120 --> 03:30.830
I’m warning you, if we're gonna call ourselves
Shin-Kawasaki, I'm seriously gonna quit.

03:31.250 --> 03:32.580
I get it already.

03:32.960 --> 03:36.250
We <i>are</i> trying to go pro...

03:38.000 --> 03:40.090
Did Momoka-san say anything after last time?

03:40.550 --> 03:41.550
Nothing.

03:42.260 --> 03:44.840
She didn't give me an answer

03:45.510 --> 03:47.350
and never brought it up again.

03:48.100 --> 03:49.690
The Cold War treatment, huh?

03:49.800 --> 03:51.640
What are you so happy about?

03:51.850 --> 03:55.150
Weird, you'd think she'd be bickering
with Nina like always if she was against it.

03:55.440 --> 03:56.860
What happened to the lizard?

03:57.190 --> 03:58.150
It’s a gecko.

03:58.320 --> 04:01.360
I moved him because he wasn't feeling well.

04:02.360 --> 04:03.240
She's pissing me off!

04:03.570 --> 04:06.200
If she has something to say,
she should just say it!

04:06.370 --> 04:07.910
And <i>you're</i> pissing off the neighbors!

04:08.410 --> 04:11.450
Well, she definitely has a right to be mad.

04:11.620 --> 04:13.750
Because Nina keeps doing
stuff behind her back.

04:14.080 --> 04:16.920
That was <i>your</i> idea.

04:17.210 --> 04:17.880
Oopsie~

04:18.250 --> 04:21.720
Just saying, if you're constantly going
to fight, Rupa and I are out.

04:22.010 --> 04:23.510
We don’t have time for this.

04:23.680 --> 04:26.550
I get it, but...

04:27.050 --> 04:30.390
So, does anyone have ideas

04:30.560 --> 04:33.020
on how to name our chaotic little band?

04:33.560 --> 04:35.810
Do you have one?
- Wait, why am I starting?

04:35.980 --> 04:37.770
You should go first.

04:37.940 --> 04:40.650
Yeah, you're the one who brought it up!

04:40.820 --> 04:43.280
Eh? It's embarrassing...

04:43.570 --> 04:46.030
How about you just say it at the same time?

04:46.780 --> 04:48.120
If you say so...

04:48.280 --> 04:50.540
Alright, on three then.

04:50.910 --> 04:51.790
Got it.

04:52.200 --> 04:53.290
One, two, three...

04:53.580 --> 04:55.080
- Chocolate.
- Undine.

04:57.330 --> 04:58.500
One, two, three...

04:58.670 --> 05:00.050
- Chocolate!
- Undine!

05:04.010 --> 05:07.050
Hey, what's wrong with Chocolate?

05:07.220 --> 05:08.390
It's...something alright.

05:08.550 --> 05:10.180
As expected from a country bumpkin.

05:10.350 --> 05:12.060
Your naming sense is gonna give me cavities.

05:12.220 --> 05:13.140
Hey, that's mean!

05:13.310 --> 05:15.020
What the heck was yours anyway? "Undine"?

05:15.190 --> 05:16.270
Well…

05:16.440 --> 05:18.560
That's <i>way</i> more embarrassing than mine.

05:18.730 --> 05:20.770
Huh? Like hell it is.

05:20.940 --> 05:22.530
They both suck.

05:22.690 --> 05:24.940
Let's hear yours then!

05:25.110 --> 05:27.320
Yeah, say it again.

05:28.490 --> 05:29.780
Dream Girl.

05:33.910 --> 05:34.830
Anything new?

05:35.460 --> 05:38.210
I never thought it'd be this hard...

05:38.540 --> 05:41.710
That's because Subaru's so picky.

05:42.090 --> 05:45.970
I'll have to take your words and
throw them right back in your face.

05:53.010 --> 05:55.100
"Did you decide on a name?"

05:56.560 --> 05:57.560
She's pissing me off.

05:59.900 --> 06:02.570
We ended up wasting the entire day.

06:08.820 --> 06:10.740
She’s late...

06:11.160 --> 06:12.240
Onee-chan?

06:13.910 --> 06:17.160
You could've sent me a message, you know.

06:17.330 --> 06:19.370
I wanted to surprise you.

06:19.670 --> 06:22.130
But I didn’t expect you’d come home <i>this</i> late.

06:22.380 --> 06:24.380
I usually come home earlier.

06:24.550 --> 06:25.880
Something came up today.

06:26.050 --> 06:27.470
Like what? You got a boyfriend?

06:29.550 --> 06:31.640
Wait, you're not working at
some shady place are you?

06:34.640 --> 06:35.600
Then what is it?

06:36.850 --> 06:37.520
A band.

06:38.940 --> 06:39.770
I'm in a band.

06:40.230 --> 06:41.060
A band?

06:42.110 --> 06:42.650
Yeah.

06:45.730 --> 06:48.650
You, in a band? Seriously?

06:48.820 --> 06:49.900
Got any pictures?

06:50.160 --> 06:50.990
Here.

06:52.820 --> 06:55.290
Woah, you were serious. You're the vocalist?

06:56.750 --> 06:58.160
What's...with this outfit?

06:58.410 --> 06:59.370
It’s a...

07:00.080 --> 07:01.250
rock outfit.

07:01.790 --> 07:02.670
A rock outfit!

07:03.290 --> 07:04.420
The heck does that mean?

07:04.590 --> 07:06.840
Just drop it.

07:07.670 --> 07:09.840
I guess that explains your
grades dropping off a cliff.

07:10.630 --> 07:11.800
How did you know?

07:11.970 --> 07:16.640
Well, schools tend to contact the family if a
student's grades drop and they start playing hooky.

07:16.810 --> 07:18.310
So they snitched on me...

07:18.480 --> 07:21.770
Be thankful I stopped your dad from coming.

07:24.730 --> 07:25.690
So, what will it be?

07:27.530 --> 07:28.780
I'm not coming back.

07:33.280 --> 07:34.160
That's fine and all,

07:34.620 --> 07:38.080
but that means you won't be able
to come back in the future either.

07:39.500 --> 07:42.960
You know, I do think it was Dad's fault.

07:48.380 --> 07:49.710
100 TIPS FOR RAISING A CHILD WELL

07:50.630 --> 07:53.970
He's a teacher who's well-known for his books on education.

07:54.340 --> 07:57.430
He couldn’t accept that his
own daughter started skipping school.

07:59.640 --> 08:02.730
I'm sure you were plenty hurt yourself,

08:03.520 --> 08:06.110
but I try to put myself in his shoes too.

08:07.110 --> 08:09.980
If you kept quiet about the bullying,

08:10.150 --> 08:11.820
the school would have owed you one.

08:12.150 --> 08:15.320
Combining that with your grades, getting a
college recommendation would be a given.

08:15.870 --> 08:17.910
Maybe, but that's not
how I want to do things.

08:18.740 --> 08:22.580
So you ran away, saying you'll get
into college through your own efforts.

08:24.870 --> 08:27.920
And now, you're neglecting your studies.

08:28.090 --> 08:30.210
Sorry, but I can't exactly
take your side on this one.

08:32.090 --> 08:37.680
A FEW DAYS LATER

08:32.970 --> 08:36.260
Let’s get moving. We're starting rehearsals tomorrow morning.

08:36.640 --> 08:37.470
Got it.

08:38.100 --> 08:39.560
Sorry I'm late.

08:40.180 --> 08:41.980
What's with the baggage?

08:42.270 --> 08:43.060
Is it too much?

08:43.230 --> 08:44.600
Show me that for a sec.

08:45.600 --> 08:47.360
This, this and this...

08:47.520 --> 08:48.940
and some clothes.

08:49.570 --> 08:50.860
Everything else stays.

08:52.030 --> 08:54.860
Always travel light.

08:56.360 --> 08:57.490
Alright then...

08:59.120 --> 09:01.870
The Chuo Expressway, right? You can-

09:02.040 --> 09:02.950
Quiet.

09:04.870 --> 09:06.830
A manual gearbox? That’s rare.

09:07.130 --> 09:11.960
It's the only thing I could find to borrow on a short notice. Let's see...

09:13.510 --> 09:14.340
I think it went like this...

09:15.380 --> 09:16.970
Or like this?

09:21.180 --> 09:23.930
Those in favor of a driver change,
please raise your hands.

09:26.940 --> 09:28.980
Rupa-san, you're a really good driver.

09:29.270 --> 09:32.480
I used to drive a lot for my part-time job.

09:32.860 --> 09:35.860
Do you think you can drive the whole way? We can take breaks if you want.

09:36.070 --> 09:38.370
Was my driving <i>that</i> bad?

09:41.410 --> 09:46.000
I’ll stop at a gas station if I
get tired, so you all can rest for now.

09:46.160 --> 09:49.250
Eh, that's a waste of a road trip...

09:49.420 --> 09:51.090
Wanna play a game then?

09:51.460 --> 09:54.300
We'll ask yes or no questions in turn,
and if everyone raises their hands you win.

09:54.460 --> 09:57.010
For example…who prefers cats over dogs?

09:57.430 --> 10:00.430
Tomo-chan, you're a dog person? Didn't see that coming.

10:00.600 --> 10:03.930
Well, they say cat-like people prefer dogs.

10:04.140 --> 10:05.520
Your turn, Nina.

10:05.850 --> 10:06.940
Umm…

10:07.690 --> 10:09.650
Who doesn't have many friends?

10:11.690 --> 10:12.610
Easy peasy.

10:13.270 --> 10:15.110
Don't just go straight for the easy ones.

10:15.690 --> 10:17.400
Momoka-san, you’re up.

10:17.820 --> 10:20.120
Eh, I don't feel like it.

10:20.910 --> 10:24.410
Fine, who thinks my driving sucks?

10:27.080 --> 10:29.920
REST AREA

10:27.870 --> 10:29.670
Let's take a short break.

10:30.540 --> 10:32.380
Alright, I'll be back in a bit.

10:38.380 --> 10:40.300
- Whoa, it's cold!
- Come on, stop it.

10:40.640 --> 10:43.300
- Let's do rock-paper-scissors.
- How much time do we have?

10:44.390 --> 10:45.430
Excuse me.

10:49.440 --> 10:50.440
You sure took your time...

10:51.520 --> 10:52.520
What is this?

10:52.690 --> 10:53.940
Did I get the wrong one?

10:55.030 --> 10:56.440
It's fine, but...

10:55.030 --> 10:58.440
TL Note : Nina got her expensive luxury brand water.

10:56.940 --> 10:57.860
Phew.

11:03.490 --> 11:06.620
Tomo-chan, why did you drop out of school?

11:07.500 --> 11:08.710
Why are you asking?

11:09.660 --> 11:11.710
Because I don't have anyone else to ask.

11:12.290 --> 11:15.420
Let’s just say I had better things to do
than waste my time in that place.

11:15.590 --> 11:17.420
My parents might as well have
not existed at that point,

11:17.590 --> 11:21.220
so I realized I'll be completely
on my own after graduating.

11:24.350 --> 11:25.510
<i>Mom?</i>

11:31.020 --> 11:34.650
She was like a completely different
person when she was with that man.

11:35.820 --> 11:38.690
Seeing her like that triggered something in me.

11:39.240 --> 11:43.490
People trying to become indie musicians
right after graduating are dime a dozen.

11:44.120 --> 11:46.330
The sooner I start, the better.

11:47.200 --> 11:50.370
So I came to Tokyo to find
people to make music with.

11:51.160 --> 11:54.250
As for school, it just took up too much time.

11:54.830 --> 11:55.630
That's all there is to it.

11:56.290 --> 11:57.420
You're amazing.

11:57.800 --> 12:01.010
I could never think that far ahead.

12:01.220 --> 12:05.680
When you suddenly lose all the people
you used to rely on, it happens naturally.

12:05.850 --> 12:08.010
When Rupa lost her family in an accident, she...

12:09.470 --> 12:11.270
also said something similar.

12:11.940 --> 12:14.270
I was...nowhere near as serious.

12:18.480 --> 12:21.400
I always wanted to do something like this!

12:21.860 --> 12:23.360
Alright, smile everyone!

12:23.530 --> 12:26.200
Momoka-san, Tomo-chan, that goes for you too.

12:26.870 --> 12:29.200
Say cheese!

12:31.790 --> 12:33.040
It's like we're idols...

12:33.540 --> 12:34.290
Please shut up.

12:35.460 --> 12:38.290
WELCOME TO THE FIREWORKS FESTIVAL LAND SUWA

12:38.800 --> 12:42.300
I know our budget's pretty
tight, but this is kinda...

12:42.800 --> 12:43.800
Ugh, it's hot.

12:45.180 --> 12:46.010
And heavy.

12:49.560 --> 12:50.810
Good morning.

12:51.140 --> 12:52.930
Good morning to you too.

12:53.770 --> 12:55.230
<i>Girls Band Cry.</i>

13:02.860 --> 13:04.200
That was pretty good, wasn't it?

13:04.530 --> 13:06.740
Are you crazy? We're all over the place.

13:06.910 --> 13:09.700
The only ones all over the place are you two.

13:09.870 --> 13:11.700
I'm playing just fine, thank you!

13:11.870 --> 13:13.410
We're all a mess.

13:13.580 --> 13:16.370
Forget that for a sec, Subaru-chan,
what's up with your head?...

13:16.620 --> 13:18.380
You saw how I slept!

13:19.040 --> 13:21.500
So, that’s your new band, Momo?

13:21.760 --> 13:22.510
"Momo"?

13:22.840 --> 13:23.470
It sure is!

13:23.630 --> 13:24.380
"It sure is"?

13:24.670 --> 13:25.930
Oh, my neck unsnapped itself.

13:26.380 --> 13:29.390
Well, I can't say you're perfect, but I like the vibe.

13:30.220 --> 13:31.970
It's better than being good but without
any chemistry, at the very least.

13:32.180 --> 13:35.310
We’ll do our best today.

13:36.440 --> 13:37.520
That guitar…

13:37.900 --> 13:39.560
Yes, it's the same one.

13:39.860 --> 13:42.150
Your sticker's still on it too.

13:41.320 --> 13:42.150
DIAMOND DUST

13:45.110 --> 13:48.910
Isn't she acting a bit...different?

13:49.070 --> 13:53.660
Or maybe this is the real Momoka-san.

13:54.160 --> 13:56.670
I’d like us to play a song together at the end.

13:56.830 --> 13:58.750
- Does that sound good?
- Really?

13:59.040 --> 14:00.840
Like, with us?

14:01.090 --> 14:03.300
Wanting to play with you is
the main reason I invited you all.

14:03.960 --> 14:06.340
Are you up for it, girls?

14:07.590 --> 14:08.590
Uh, yes.

14:08.930 --> 14:11.970
How about a little session then?

14:12.140 --> 14:14.720
- Session?
- She means singing together.

14:15.600 --> 14:17.230
You’re the vocalist, right?

14:17.520 --> 14:18.140
Yes, I am.

14:19.690 --> 14:24.400
<i>Farewell, melody of the past</i>

14:24.570 --> 14:28.990
<i>Until we meet again</i>

14:29.450 --> 14:31.700
<i>As we become adults</i>

14:31.870 --> 14:33.990
<i>Just once more</i>

14:34.330 --> 14:38.750
<i>As our memories fade</i>

14:40.040 --> 14:41.000
- What do you think?
- Huh?

14:41.380 --> 14:42.920
- Can you sing it?
- I think so.

14:43.090 --> 14:44.460
Probably.

14:44.920 --> 14:45.760
I’ll do my best.

14:46.800 --> 14:49.260
That's settled then. I’ll tell the manager.

14:52.100 --> 14:53.970
- Great song, wasn't it?
- Yes!

14:54.680 --> 14:59.310
I saw Mine's concert not long after I
came to Tokyo for the first time.

15:01.600 --> 15:03.610
She was just a no-name supporting act like us, an afterthought.

15:04.480 --> 15:08.150
And yet she didn't let that faze her one bit,
singing with all she had as if she was fighting.

15:09.070 --> 15:11.610
"This is true rock", I thought to myself back then.

15:12.820 --> 15:15.370
It's the perfect scenario for my final concert.

15:19.160 --> 15:21.330
I decided to leave the band.

15:21.500 --> 15:23.210
Tomorrow's concert is the end for me.

15:23.590 --> 15:24.630
I'm out.

15:25.500 --> 15:27.170
What are you saying?

15:27.800 --> 15:32.550
Sorry, but I don’t have it in me to go pro again.

15:32.800 --> 15:33.890
Why?

15:34.050 --> 15:37.930
My songs aren't made for the big world.

15:38.390 --> 15:42.810
I'm truly happy that you grew to like them,

15:43.100 --> 15:47.070
and even more so that they sparked a fire
in you. Seriously, thank you.

15:47.230 --> 15:48.440
Are you really okay with this?

15:48.860 --> 15:49.490
Yep.

15:53.110 --> 15:54.030
This is my answer.

15:54.370 --> 15:57.700
NICHOME

15:58.620 --> 16:01.500
Wow, I didn't expect you to drink that much!

16:05.790 --> 16:07.960
Rupa-san, you sure can hold your liquor!

16:08.670 --> 16:10.670
She loves drinking people under the table...

16:10.840 --> 16:15.600
Don't tell me we have to carry her again…
She's pretty damn heavy, for how she looks at least.

16:16.390 --> 16:18.600
You better not mess up tomorrow.

16:18.930 --> 16:21.270
We owe the audience that much.

16:21.430 --> 16:23.980
- I know that.
- What's with the surly faces?

16:25.480 --> 16:26.980
What is it? Are we fighting?

16:29.980 --> 16:34.070
Uh, that aside! Mine-san, what kind of music do you like?

16:34.320 --> 16:37.620
Mine-san, have you ever
thought about quitting music?

16:37.870 --> 16:40.200
Oh come on, where did that come from?

16:40.540 --> 16:41.960
Cut it out, will ya?

16:43.040 --> 16:45.880
No one likes having to
make these kinds of decisions.

16:46.880 --> 16:50.670
The longer you keep at something, the clearer your prospects at it become.

16:50.960 --> 16:54.800
If you fail the first time around, you can chalk it up to bad luck.

16:54.970 --> 16:58.510
But the second time, you
start questioning your ability.

16:59.720 --> 17:02.770
So...she lost the ability to believe that things will go well?

17:05.520 --> 17:07.230
She wants to believe.

17:07.860 --> 17:11.780
But the more you believe in your success,
the more painful it will be when you fail.

17:12.360 --> 17:13.280
She's scared.

17:14.070 --> 17:16.450
She's scared, because music is everything to her.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.410
Well, I'll be counting on you tomorrow.

17:24.580 --> 17:25.170
Excuse me!

17:27.380 --> 17:29.840
Are you...not scared of the same thing?

17:30.420 --> 17:31.090
Me?

17:31.420 --> 17:32.090
Yes.

17:35.430 --> 17:36.720
Of course I am.

17:37.090 --> 17:40.430
Sometimes to the point where I can't even eat or sleep.

17:40.810 --> 17:41.680
Even now?

17:42.100 --> 17:42.970
Of course.

17:43.140 --> 17:47.440
But that's what it means to turn
your passion into your profession.

17:47.980 --> 17:49.770
When I was studying music at college,

17:49.940 --> 17:53.070
I thought about becoming a teacher and singing as an amateur.

17:54.280 --> 17:57.820
I thought it was the smartest choice.

17:59.280 --> 18:01.280
What made you change your mind?

18:01.700 --> 18:02.910
Good question.

18:03.500 --> 18:05.250
I don't even remember anymore.

18:06.040 --> 18:06.830
Really?

18:08.830 --> 18:12.960
Anyway, for me the stage is a place where I can express myself wholeheartedly.

18:13.340 --> 18:14.510
A place I truly love.

18:15.170 --> 18:18.340
So I must've thought
something along the lines of

18:19.090 --> 18:21.220
"It doesn't matter how difficult
or painful it might be sometimes".

18:24.350 --> 18:25.980
Oi!

18:28.190 --> 18:30.190
Ew, you reek of alcohol!

18:30.360 --> 18:33.270
What're you babblin' about?
I haven't had a single drop!

18:33.440 --> 18:35.610
How does that lie even come out of your mouth?!

18:35.990 --> 18:38.200
You're a real pain, you know...

18:38.360 --> 18:40.320
You're always, always...

18:40.490 --> 18:42.370
See you.

18:43.950 --> 18:46.830
Oi, you listenin' to me?

18:47.710 --> 18:49.460
I'm leaving her to you!

18:50.130 --> 18:51.960
Huh? Hey, what am I supposed
to do with this?!

18:52.460 --> 18:55.050
Nina! This isn't fair!

18:57.050 --> 18:59.090
Excuse me, do you know how I can get to the lake?

19:00.800 --> 19:02.600
Thank you very much!

19:17.440 --> 19:18.360
That's it.

19:19.240 --> 19:19.990
I know what to do now.

19:20.320 --> 19:24.120
I've made my decision!

19:35.340 --> 19:36.170
I'm going to do it.

19:38.420 --> 19:41.260
KAMISUWA KAICHO

19:43.850 --> 19:44.720
<i>Thank you!</i>

19:45.180 --> 19:48.270
<i>The next band is my personal favorite,
so give them a warm welcome alright?</i>

19:51.690 --> 19:52.270
Ready?

19:52.730 --> 19:53.520
Ready.

19:54.020 --> 19:56.860
By the way, what about our name?

19:57.360 --> 19:58.280
Did you decide on one in the end?

19:58.690 --> 20:01.820
We were supposed to come up with
something while eating, but no luck.

20:02.280 --> 20:06.160
If we're gonna call ourselves Shin-Kawasaki,
I'm gonna...oh whatever.

20:08.120 --> 20:08.660
Huh?

20:09.450 --> 20:10.410
Good evening!

20:10.660 --> 20:12.420
- We are…
- That little...

20:13.670 --> 20:14.500
Uh, we are…

20:22.090 --> 20:23.300
**TOGENASHI TOGEARI**

20:25.050 --> 20:26.760
We're TOGENASHI TOGEARI!

20:28.470 --> 20:30.980
They have the same name as my T-shirt.

20:31.180 --> 20:33.190
What a coincidence, wow.

20:34.850 --> 20:35.900
Nice to meet you all.

20:36.230 --> 20:39.820
I joined the band this spring.

20:40.400 --> 20:43.360
I don't know what pushed me to do it,

20:43.530 --> 20:45.490
or why I wanted to sing in the first place.

20:45.820 --> 20:47.450
But I love it.

20:47.950 --> 20:51.200
For the first time in my life, I could lose myself in something.

20:53.040 --> 20:54.210
Let's hurry.

20:55.210 --> 20:59.000
You know, there's a song that changed my life.

20:59.340 --> 21:02.720
That song became my drive to move forward.

21:03.680 --> 21:07.800
And I want to prove to the world that it has value,

21:08.180 --> 21:10.350
that it can touch people's hearts.

21:10.520 --> 21:12.980
I want to tell everyone how amazing it is.

21:13.480 --> 21:17.360
Subaru-chan, Rupa-san, Tomo-chan, and Momoka-san

21:17.900 --> 21:20.190
I'm sure all of them feel
that way about something too.

21:20.900 --> 21:22.820
That's why we're giving it everything we have.

21:23.320 --> 21:25.910
We're scared, but we don't give up.

21:26.780 --> 21:28.030
And that's why I…

21:28.620 --> 21:29.620
I-

21:31.750 --> 21:32.750
People might get annoyed, you know.

21:34.460 --> 21:35.250
If you keep going on about yourself.

21:36.210 --> 21:36.790
Sorry.

21:40.710 --> 21:41.550
Geez.

21:41.710 --> 21:44.090
That's one hell of an entrance.

21:44.670 --> 21:45.630
Well, whatever!

21:48.350 --> 21:53.060
<i>I am a mass of wounds, body and mind fragmented by wear and tear</i>

21:53.480 --> 21:58.610
<i>A chimeric passion in tatters in my ribcage</i>

22:08.990 --> 22:13.750
<i>A trip to a deceptive city, like a lost soul, I wander</i>

22:14.080 --> 22:18.380
<i>In a spiral of stench and noise, I cry</i>

22:18.830 --> 22:21.290
<i>How to overcome today when everything is darkness?</i>

22:21.460 --> 22:23.840
<i>Stop losing yourself in trivialities</i>

22:24.010 --> 22:29.640
<i>This voice resonates in me as my tears keep flowing</i>

22:29.800 --> 22:32.220
<i>"Conquer your fear and stop hiding"</i>

22:32.390 --> 22:34.770
<i>"Join me so we can dance"</i>

22:34.930 --> 22:37.850
<i>I want to leave this disgusting world</i>

22:38.560 --> 22:39.730
<i>To scatter violently</i>

22:40.150 --> 22:42.480
<i>To scatter, scatter slowly</i>

22:42.690 --> 22:44.730
<i>But don't abandon me to my fate</i>

22:44.900 --> 22:49.200
<i>As one vomits their sadness into the measures of a chorus</i>

22:49.410 --> 22:52.780
<i>Forever, again and again</i>

22:52.990 --> 22:55.120
<i>Until love is stronger</i>

22:55.330 --> 22:59.330
<i>I refuse to believe it is just an emotion</i>

22:59.500 --> 23:03.090
<i>To the point of losing my mind</i>

23:30.110 --> 23:30.700
<i>Rupa-san.</i>

23:31.660 --> 23:32.530
<i>Tomo-chan.</i>

23:33.530 --> 23:34.530
<i>Subaru-chan.</i>

23:35.700 --> 23:36.750
<i>Momoka-san.</i>

23:38.000 --> 23:38.870
<i>I'm...</i>

23:40.210 --> 23:41.580
<i>I'm dropping out of school.</i>

23:47.510 --> 23:49.880
<i>To be continued: "If You Needed to Cry."</i>
